  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Leveraging Fiscal Policy to Reduce Inequality in Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As part of the commitment towards achieving the Sustainable Development Goal (SDG)10.4.2, each country is expected to monitor not only their level of income inequality, but also the impact of their fiscal policies on inequality. Currently, there exist only one data set for Ghana on inequality, produced in 2015 using 2012 data by the Commitment to Equity(CEQ) Institute. To meet Ghana&apos;s obligation under the indicators for this goal (SDG10.4.2), more groundwork needs to be done to mainstream the methodology within government, while also mobilizing civil society. This project will leverage the Ghanaian government&apos;s adoption of a SDG framework for the national budget and economic policy. This project will take place within the context of Ghana&apos;s Beyond Aid and Sustainable Development Goals agenda and will seek to get government working with civil society and other relevant actors to regularly analyse and publish the SDG10.4.2 indicator in accessible and understandable format for policy making and demonstrate commitment to reducing social and economic inequality and to enhance equitable, sustainable and inclusive development.</narrative>
  </description>
